; autumn_trial.room - the autumn song trials (docs/maps/README.md), left to right.
; Tested by tests/scenes/world/rooms/trials/autumn_trial_test.gd. Sized for base
; movement: the trials grant no skills. Soltar's pulse is small on purpose
; (release_pulse_stats.tres, 288 px): its radius is how it chooses.
;
; 1. The trail under the leaves (design 02 section 8, Outono Espacial 1): a
;    curtain of dry leaves closes the only way through the stone. Soltar drops
;    it; the grey grows it back.
; 2. Pushed by the gale (Outono Espacial 2): a 16-cell chasm over water with a
;    natural current. Neither a running jump (8.5 cells), nor the current alone
;    (about 12), nor the gale alone (about 15) clears it - played three cells
;    back from the edge, the gale ADDS to the current and carries the jump
;    across (about 17).
; 3. The counterweights (Outono Logico 1): two loads hang over two plates, high
;    enough to walk under (their bottoms at 64 px) and low enough that their
;    tops are no step up to the lift's shelf (256 px). The
;    right one (col 55) raises the lift to the shelf; the wrong one (col 39)
;    jams it down. Played between them, Soltar reaches both - stand by the one
;    you mean.
; 4. The load on the wind (Outono Logico 2): a cocoon hangs over a high shelf
;    with a plate at its far end, and the plate opens the last gate. Soltar
;    drops it on the shelf; Vendaval from the left blows it to the plate. The
;    other way round, the wind has nothing to push. Carried out of Soltar's
;    disc it is in the grey again, and the grey hangs it back on its rope - so
;    Soltar is played under the middle of the shelf (col 64), where its disc
;    covers both the rope and the plate. A stone stop at the shelf's end keeps
;    the gale from blowing it on past the plate and off. Its shelf is
;    low (160 px) so the cocoon is in view from the floor; the stone wall
;    before it keeps every step from the counterweights away.

